---
// The traceability chain from the melt to the motor: each step, the identity it carries, and the document that links it.
const ink = 'var(--rd-ink)', muted = 'var(--rd-muted)', blue = 'var(--rd-blue)', ok = 'var(--rd-ok)', accent = 'var(--rd-accent)';
const steps = [
  ['Melt', 'heat 41872', ['producer certificate:', 'chemistry, melt practice']],
  ['Bar, plate, billet', 'heat 41872', ['producer certificate:', 'properties as delivered']],
  ['Distributor cuts it', 'heat on each piece', ['distributor certificate', '+ producer certificate']],
  ['Forge and machine', 'work order, part no.', ['router: each operation', 'signed and dated']],
  ['Heat treatment', 'furnace load 2291', ['heat-treatment cert,', 'furnace chart, coupons']],
  ['Inspection and NDT', 'serial number 017', ['NDT and dimensional', 'reports, FAI']],
  ['Motor assembly', 'motor serial 004', ['build record: which', 'serials in which motor']],
] as const;
const top = 34, rowH = 50, bx = 26, bw = 138, dx = 172, dw = 158;
---

<figure class="viz tracechain">
  <p class="viz-title">One chain, from the melt to the motor</p>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 360 400" role="img" aria-labelledby="tracechain-desc" style="max-width: 520px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <desc id="tracechain-desc">
      Seven steps from top to bottom: melt, mill product, distributor, forging and machining, heat treatment, inspection
      and NDT, and motor assembly. Each step carries an identity (heat number, work order, furnace load, serial number)
      and has a document that links it to the step before. Tracing back goes from the motor to the melt; tracing forward
      goes from a bad heat to every motor that contains it.
    </desc>
    <defs>
      <marker id="tc-arr" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="context-stroke"></path></marker>
    </defs>
    <text x={bx + bw / 2} y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill={muted}>step and identity</text>
    <text x={dx + dw / 2} y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill={muted}>document that links it</text>
    {steps.map(([n, id, doc], k) => (
      <g>
        <rect x={bx} y={top + k * rowH} width={bw} height="36" rx="5" fill="var(--rd-panel)" stroke={ink} stroke-width="1"></rect>
        <text x={bx + 8} y={top + k * rowH + 15} font-size="11.5" fill={ink}>{n}</text>
        <text x={bx + 8} y={top + k * rowH + 29} font-size="10" fill={blue}>{id}</text>
        <line x1={bx + bw} y1={top + k * rowH + 18} x2={dx - 2} y2={top + k * rowH + 18} stroke={muted} stroke-dasharray="2 2"></line>
        <text x={dx} y={top + k * rowH + 15} font-size="10" fill={muted}>{doc[0]}</text>
        <text x={dx} y={top + k * rowH + 29} font-size="10" fill={muted}>{doc[1]}</text>
        {k < steps.length - 1 && <line x1={bx + bw / 2} y1={top + k * rowH + 36} x2={bx + bw / 2} y2={top + (k + 1) * rowH - 1} stroke={ink} stroke-width="1.2" marker-end="url(#tc-arr)"></line>}
      </g>
    ))}
    <line x1="19" y1={top + 6 * rowH + 30} x2="19" y2={top + 4} stroke={ok} stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#tc-arr)"></line>
    <text x="10" y={top + 3 * rowH + 18} text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill={ok} transform={`rotate(-90 10 ${top + 3 * rowH + 18})`}>trace back</text>
    <line x1="333" y1={top + 4} x2="333" y2={top + 6 * rowH + 30} stroke={accent} stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#tc-arr)"></line>
    <text x="344" y={top + 3 * rowH + 18} text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill={accent} transform={`rotate(90 344 ${top + 3 * rowH + 18})`}>trace forward</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    Tracing back answers "what is this part made of, and how was it processed?". Tracing forward answers "this heat is
    bad: which motors contain it?". Each identity must be on the material or the part at each step, and each document
    must give the identity before and after the step. One break, such as an offcut without its heat number, breaks the
    chain for everything after it.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
